1
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:58,000
"Not Yours"

2
00:00:58,100 --> 00:01:00,800
(Episode 4)

3
00:01:10,799 --> 00:01:11,799
Think you're tough, huh?

4
00:01:12,640 --> 00:01:13,640
Young Master!

5
00:01:15,400 --> 00:01:16,400
You coward!

6
00:01:16,519 --> 00:01:18,239
Fight me one-on-one if you've got the guts!

7
00:01:18,519 --> 00:01:19,920
Ganging up on someone is pathetic!

8
00:01:20,400 --> 00:01:21,400
Let him go!

9
00:01:21,680 --> 00:01:22,680
One-on-one? Let's go!

10
00:01:25,599 --> 00:01:26,599
Young Master!

11
00:01:30,760 --> 00:01:31,760
Boss P'Eng!

12
00:01:31,959 --> 00:01:32,959
Stop fighting!

13
00:01:33,079 --> 00:01:34,079
Everyone, stand down!

14
00:01:40,159 --> 00:01:41,200
Please let him go.

15
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:44,400
I'll go with you.

16
00:01:45,239 --> 00:01:46,680
I'll take full responsibility.

17
00:01:52,159 --> 00:01:52,959
You can't go with him!

18
00:01:52,959 --> 00:01:53,959
You still have your brother
and sister to look after!

19
00:01:53,960 --> 00:01:55,160
Are you alright, Young Master?

20
00:02:00,840 --> 00:02:02,319
My mom texted me.

21
00:02:03,840 --> 00:02:05,239
She took the ring.

22
00:02:05,879 --> 00:02:07,959
Your mother admitted it?

23
00:02:16,240 --> 00:02:17,240
I'll go with you.

24
00:02:18,800 --> 00:02:20,240
I'll take full responsibility.

25
00:02:20,520 --> 00:02:21,039
No!

26
00:02:21,240 --> 00:02:22,240
You can't go with him.

27
00:02:22,319 --> 00:02:22,639
You...

28
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:24,158
You really can't go with him!

29
00:02:24,159 --> 00:02:25,159
Boss P'Eng,

30
00:02:25,599 --> 00:02:27,400
we were just messing around the other day.

31
00:02:27,560 --> 00:02:29,159
He's my best friend from college.

32
00:02:29,680 --> 00:02:31,895
Even though there are some
misunderstandings between us,

33
00:02:31,919 --> 00:02:33,479
could you please let it slide,

34
00:02:33,879 --> 00:02:34,999
just this once, for my sake?

35
00:02:41,039 --> 00:02:42,039
Fine.

36
00:02:42,159 --> 00:02:43,399
I'll do this as a favor to you.

37
00:02:43,840 --> 00:02:44,840
Thank you, Boss P'Eng.

38
00:02:45,159 --> 00:02:46,159
Mm.

39
00:02:47,319 --> 00:02:48,319
A Pong,

40
00:02:49,120 --> 00:02:50,158
please do me a favor.

41
00:02:50,159 --> 00:02:51,799
Go look after Xiaotong and Xiaoya.

42
00:02:51,800 --> 00:02:53,240
Just tell them...

43
00:02:54,439 --> 00:02:56,399
Tell them their big brother
got a well-paying job

44
00:02:58,439 --> 00:02:59,960
and has to go out of town for a while.

45
00:03:00,759 --> 00:03:02,359
Tell them to be good.

46
00:03:02,360 --> 00:03:03,680
I'll be back as soon as I can,

47
00:03:04,080 --> 00:03:06,520
and I'll take them to the
amusement park when I get back.

48
00:03:09,800 --> 00:03:11,439
I promise I'll be back soon.

49
00:03:16,639 --> 00:03:18,639
I'm sorry, Boss.

50
00:03:20,159 --> 00:03:21,919
I need to take an
extended leave of absence.

51
00:03:23,599 --> 00:03:24,599
Right.

52
00:03:26,639 --> 00:03:27,639
A Pong,

53
00:03:27,800 --> 00:03:29,439
there are buns I made in the fridge.

54
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:31,439
That should last you guys a while.

55
00:03:41,159 --> 00:03:42,159
Let's go.

56
00:03:47,759 --> 00:03:48,759
Don't worry about me.

57
00:03:50,120 --> 00:03:51,320
I'll come back safe and sound.

58
00:04:07,479 --> 00:04:08,000
Boss,

59
00:04:08,080 --> 00:04:09,080
Yes?

60
00:04:09,120 --> 00:04:10,400
All the bills here,

61
00:04:10,479 --> 00:04:12,199
plus any damages, are on me.

62
00:04:13,280 --> 00:04:15,240
I'll have Mingkun settle
it with you in a moment.

63
00:04:15,319 --> 00:04:16,560
Understood.

64
00:04:20,480 --> 00:04:22,000
Since Milan is letting it slide,

65
00:04:22,439 --> 00:04:23,959
I won't waste my breath on you either.

66
00:04:30,120 --> 00:04:31,120
Young man,

67
00:04:31,839 --> 00:04:33,120
don't get too arrogant...

68
00:04:35,600 --> 00:04:38,480
until you have the leverage to back it up.

69
00:04:43,879 --> 00:04:44,879
Mr. Milan,

70
00:04:45,240 --> 00:04:46,040
I have other business,

71
00:04:46,199 --> 00:04:47,199
so I'll be heading back.

72
00:04:47,720 --> 00:04:48,720
If you need anything,

73
00:04:48,839 --> 00:04:50,000
just contact me directly.

74
00:04:50,800 --> 00:04:52,079
Of course. Take care.

75
00:04:52,680 --> 00:04:54,520
Thank you for showing
mercy today, Boss P'Eng.

76
00:05:06,639 --> 00:05:07,639
Don't go after him.

77
00:05:08,240 --> 00:05:09,240
Let him go.

78
00:05:09,800 --> 00:05:10,800
Trust me.

79
00:05:11,519 --> 00:05:13,600
Boss P'Eng isn't a bad person deep down.

80
00:05:13,920 --> 00:05:15,318
He won't hurt your friend.

81
00:05:15,319 --> 00:05:16,319
Mm.

82
00:05:21,040 --> 00:05:22,040
Mm.

83
00:05:29,800 --> 00:05:32,879
You claimed you could work
for me to pay off the debt.

84
00:05:35,839 --> 00:05:36,839
Let's hear the details.

85
00:05:38,040 --> 00:05:39,040
What should I say?

86
00:05:40,600 --> 00:05:41,759
Be specific.

87
00:05:42,600 --> 00:05:45,040
Like how exactly do you plan to pay it off?

88
00:05:49,279 --> 00:05:50,360
I can do housework,

89
00:05:51,480 --> 00:05:52,480
cook,

90
00:05:53,319 --> 00:05:54,399
and tend to the flowerbeds.

91
00:05:54,759 --> 00:05:56,160
I can do all of that.

92
00:05:56,519 --> 00:05:57,519
That's it?

93
00:06:02,120 --> 00:06:03,120
Yeah.

94
00:06:04,600 --> 00:06:05,759
Do you have any idea

95
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:08,639
how much the diamond ring
your mother stole is worth?

96
00:06:12,079 --> 00:06:13,639
The price tag would scare you to death.

97
00:06:14,480 --> 00:06:17,160
It might be an amount you
couldn't pay off in your entire lifetime.

98
00:06:22,560 --> 00:06:23,920
Putting that aside,

99
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:27,480
you claim you can clean and cook.

100
00:06:28,680 --> 00:06:31,000
I have professional
maids and chefs at home.

101
00:06:31,720 --> 00:06:32,800
At best,

102
00:06:33,560 --> 00:06:35,920
you'd just tend to that flowerbed
your mother looked after.

103
00:06:38,839 --> 00:06:41,959
Do you really think that's
enough to clear your debt?

104
00:06:46,319 --> 00:06:47,759
Then what do you want?

105
00:06:48,319 --> 00:06:49,319
What I want?

106
00:06:56,240 --> 00:06:59,600
Shouldn't you know best what I
want, deep down in your heart?

107
00:07:01,839 --> 00:07:03,439
I'm not a mind reader.

108
00:07:03,720 --> 00:07:04,920
How on earth would I know?

109
00:07:14,040 --> 00:07:15,720
You agreed to come back with me.

110
00:07:17,399 --> 00:07:18,639
I thought

111
00:07:20,680 --> 00:07:22,520
you were already prepared
for what that meant.

112
00:07:30,240 --> 00:07:31,240
What?

113
00:07:31,399 --> 00:07:33,480
Still playing dumb with me?

114
00:07:36,319 --> 00:07:37,439
I'm not playing dumb.

115
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:39,040
I genuinely don't know.

116
00:08:02,480 --> 00:08:03,199
Boss,

117
00:08:03,279 --> 00:08:04,279
please show some decency.

118
00:08:06,480 --> 00:08:07,560
Decency?

119
00:08:09,079 --> 00:08:11,879
That word doesn't exist in my dictionary.

120
00:08:14,160 --> 00:08:15,160
Besides,

121
00:08:16,040 --> 00:08:17,518
what right do you have

122
00:08:17,519 --> 00:08:18,879
to preach decency to me right now?

123
00:08:20,399 --> 00:08:21,800
I know where I stand.

124
00:08:22,240 --> 00:08:23,399
The things you're good at,

125
00:08:23,560 --> 00:08:24,560
I can't do.

126
00:08:25,160 --> 00:08:26,976
And what I'm good at,
you wouldn't want to do.

127
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:28,360
We both chose this.

128
00:08:38,559 --> 00:08:39,559
Go on.

129
00:08:40,720 --> 00:08:42,000
If you chose me,

130
00:08:42,759 --> 00:08:44,399
it means I, Pao Bei, am worth it.

131
00:08:44,799 --> 00:08:46,199
It's not about being worthy or not.

132
00:08:46,600 --> 00:08:47,879
If you think I'm not worth it,

133
00:08:48,320 --> 00:08:49,720
then turn me over to the police.

134
00:08:53,559 --> 00:08:54,600
Not bad.

135
00:08:59,200 --> 00:09:00,519
You've got some nerve, kid.

136
00:09:01,240 --> 00:09:02,720
You really do.

137
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:04,000
Mm.

138
00:09:13,919 --> 00:09:16,200
Take care of this guy.

139
00:09:16,559 --> 00:09:17,559
Understood, Master.

140
00:09:17,759 --> 00:09:19,200
His room has been arranged.

141
00:09:19,360 --> 00:09:20,720
Your bath has been drawn as well.

142
00:09:21,159 --> 00:09:22,000
Please get some rest.

143
00:09:22,001 --> 00:09:23,159
I'll handle the rest.

144
00:09:37,600 --> 00:09:38,798
I told you,

145
00:09:38,799 --> 00:09:40,176
the roads around here are rough like this.

146
00:09:40,200 --> 00:09:41,840
I told you not to come, but you insisted.

147
00:09:43,679 --> 00:09:44,679
I just wanted to see

148
00:09:44,680 --> 00:09:46,200
where you and Pao Bei live.

149
00:09:50,120 --> 00:09:51,120
What is there to see?

150
00:09:52,039 --> 00:09:53,919
You're a big celebrity now.

151
00:09:54,799 --> 00:09:56,559
How could you possibly understand

152
00:09:57,120 --> 00:09:58,960
the struggles of
working-class people like us?

153
00:10:01,360 --> 00:10:02,799
So what if I'm a star?

154
00:10:03,840 --> 00:10:05,080
Celebrities are human too.

155
00:10:11,159 --> 00:10:12,159
Come here.

156
00:10:12,639 --> 00:10:13,639
Huh?

157
00:10:25,919 --> 00:10:27,279
Look at our shadows on the wall.

158
00:10:28,600 --> 00:10:29,600
Aren't they the same?

159
00:11:17,200 --> 00:11:18,200
Want a smoke?

160
00:11:18,679 --> 00:11:19,679
No thanks.

161
00:11:20,440 --> 00:11:22,679
Smoking is bad for my voice and skin.

162
00:11:27,840 --> 00:11:29,079
I wonder who it was

163
00:11:29,080 --> 00:11:30,816
that taught others to
smoke in the first place,

164
00:11:30,840 --> 00:11:32,000
only to quit first.

165
00:11:33,799 --> 00:11:35,399
I was young and dumb back then.

166
00:11:42,759 --> 00:11:43,759
What are you staring at?

167
00:11:48,200 --> 00:11:49,440
It feels like over the years,

168
00:11:49,919 --> 00:11:51,679
you and Pao Bei have had it pretty rough.

169
00:11:54,720 --> 00:11:55,720
And you haven't?

170
00:11:57,000 --> 00:11:58,000
Me?

171
00:11:58,480 --> 00:11:59,759
I've been alright.

172
00:12:01,360 --> 00:12:02,840
What's so hard about being a celebrity?

173
00:12:06,399 --> 00:12:07,399
Right.

174
00:12:07,960 --> 00:12:10,000
I mean, it can be tough,

175
00:12:10,480 --> 00:12:12,320
but at least I make more
money than you guys.

176
00:12:13,480 --> 00:12:14,480
Fair point.

177
00:12:16,120 --> 00:12:17,120
So...

178
00:12:17,919 --> 00:12:20,879
how did you get those injuries from before?

179
00:12:32,440 --> 00:12:33,799
Training injuries.

180
00:12:37,799 --> 00:12:38,959
But that's all behind me now.

181
00:12:39,679 --> 00:12:40,080
Hey,

182
00:12:40,360 --> 00:12:41,559
you're something else.

183
00:12:42,080 --> 00:12:44,160
What made you think to
smear soy sauce all over?

184
00:12:44,919 --> 00:12:46,359
If that really was Boss P'Eng,

185
00:12:46,360 --> 00:12:47,720
you'd be in serious trouble.

186
00:12:48,799 --> 00:12:49,879
So what if I would've been?

187
00:12:50,360 --> 00:12:51,399
I, Jiang Weibang,

188
00:12:51,559 --> 00:12:52,879
believe in an eye for an ear!

189
00:12:54,679 --> 00:12:56,639
My idioms might be a little rusty,

190
00:12:57,120 --> 00:13:00,279
but isn't it 'an eye for an eye'?

191
00:13:02,240 --> 00:13:03,559
So what if I'm uneducated?

192
00:13:03,600 --> 00:13:04,600
Got a problem with that?

193
00:13:05,399 --> 00:13:05,919
Not at all.

194
00:13:06,159 --> 00:13:07,159
Whatever works for you.

195
00:13:08,919 --> 00:13:13,519
What if that boss also
believes in 'an eye for an ear'?

196
00:13:14,366 --> 00:13:16,840
Me, scared of him?
Who have I ever been afraid of?

197
00:13:18,399 --> 00:13:20,360
Weren't you pretty scared of me back then?

198
00:13:22,159 --> 00:13:23,799
Scared of you? In your dreams!

199
00:13:24,399 --> 00:13:25,399
Hey,

200
00:13:25,559 --> 00:13:28,320
who was it that got hammered
and cried about being afraid I'd leave?

201
00:13:28,720 --> 00:13:29,279
Hey!

202
00:13:29,679 --> 00:13:31,000
Don't talk nonsense!

203
00:13:31,240 --> 00:13:33,200
When did I ever say something that sappy?

204
00:13:33,360 --> 00:13:33,919
No way.

205
00:13:34,320 --> 00:13:35,320
Absolutely impossible!

206
00:13:38,823 --> 00:13:41,923
[A letter informing Milan that he has
breached his contract and has to cooperate]

207
00:13:48,480 --> 00:13:49,480
What's wrong?

208
00:13:51,519 --> 00:13:52,480
In a bad mood?

209
00:13:52,481 --> 00:13:54,320
It's nothing, just work stuff.

210
00:13:54,919 --> 00:13:55,919
Let's hurry.

211
00:13:56,399 --> 00:13:57,959
Didn't Pao Bei ask you
to take care of his siblings?

212
00:13:57,960 --> 00:13:58,960
Don't keep them waiting.

213
00:13:59,039 --> 00:14:00,039
Right.

214
00:14:24,399 --> 00:14:27,039
I've been on my feet all day
without a single bite to eat.

215
00:14:58,360 --> 00:14:59,559
Whatever.

216
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:01,880
You don't feel hungry
when you're drunk anyway.

217
00:15:35,600 --> 00:15:36,879
Who is it?

218
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:53,159
What's up?

219
00:15:53,559 --> 00:15:54,559
Finally come around?

220
00:15:56,159 --> 00:15:57,200
Let me in.

221
00:15:57,879 --> 00:15:59,360
I'm not done talking yet.

222
00:16:20,600 --> 00:16:21,600
Go ahead.

223
00:16:22,159 --> 00:16:24,159
What else do you have to add?

224
00:16:24,759 --> 00:16:26,399
The money my mom owes you,

225
00:16:27,200 --> 00:16:28,559
I will definitely pay you back.

226
00:16:30,039 --> 00:16:32,159
But please leave my friend A Pong alone,

227
00:16:32,519 --> 00:16:33,759
and my brother and sister too.

228
00:16:36,240 --> 00:16:38,799
Your friend brought this on himself.

229
00:16:39,960 --> 00:16:41,398
That and your mother owing me money

230
00:16:41,399 --> 00:16:42,799
are two entirely different things.

231
00:16:45,879 --> 00:16:46,879
Fine.

232
00:16:47,360 --> 00:16:49,360
Then could you please
spare my brother and sister?

233
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:53,360
Let them live and go to school in peace.

234
00:16:57,080 --> 00:16:59,279
No.

235
00:17:10,480 --> 00:17:12,400
What are you glaring at me for?

236
00:17:17,279 --> 00:17:18,400
Tell me.

237
00:17:19,880 --> 00:17:21,920
How do you plan to pay me back?

238
00:17:36,720 --> 00:17:38,160
I'm asking you.

239
00:17:38,559 --> 00:17:40,119
How will you pay me back?

240
00:17:42,599 --> 00:17:45,079
What do you even have?

241
00:17:52,200 --> 00:17:54,400
Even the clothes on your back

242
00:17:55,799 --> 00:17:57,440
belong to me.

243
00:18:09,440 --> 00:18:10,440
Face it.

244
00:18:10,839 --> 00:18:12,400
You have nothing.

245
00:18:13,039 --> 00:18:14,559
Just work it off here slowly

246
00:18:14,759 --> 00:18:16,279
and earn your keep,

247
00:18:17,319 --> 00:18:18,759
so that thief of a mother of yours...

248
00:18:18,920 --> 00:18:19,920
What did you say?

249
00:18:22,839 --> 00:18:23,759
What do I have?

250
00:18:23,799 --> 00:18:25,119
Tonight, I'll show you

251
00:18:26,759 --> 00:18:27,759
what I have.

252
00:19:10,319 --> 00:19:11,319
What's the matter?

253
00:19:12,440 --> 00:19:13,799
Don't even know how to kiss?

254
00:19:17,240 --> 00:19:19,400
Don't tell me it's your
first time kissing a guy?

255
00:19:29,519 --> 00:19:31,279
Show me what you've got.

256
00:19:32,440 --> 00:19:33,920
Is this really all you have?

257
00:20:28,759 --> 00:20:30,000
What are you doing with that?

258
00:20:43,559 --> 00:20:44,559
Get out.

259
00:20:48,039 --> 00:20:49,039
Get out!

260
00:21:14,480 --> 00:21:15,480
Hey...

261
00:21:18,960 --> 00:21:20,480
What on earth am I doing?

262
00:21:23,359 --> 00:21:24,439
Still up this late?

263
00:21:24,440 --> 00:21:25,560
What are you doing out here?

264
00:21:29,039 --> 00:21:30,039
I...

265
00:21:30,359 --> 00:21:31,359
I got lost.

266
00:21:33,200 --> 00:21:34,239
Don't wander around at night.

267
00:21:34,240 --> 00:21:35,559
You might run into trouble.

268
00:21:36,160 --> 00:21:37,160
Come back with me.

269
00:21:40,480 --> 00:21:41,000
By the way,

270
00:21:41,359 --> 00:21:42,518
the Master instructed me

271
00:21:42,519 --> 00:21:43,599
to confiscate your phone.

272
00:21:44,640 --> 00:21:45,640
Why is he doing this?

273
00:21:47,480 --> 00:21:48,896
Don't I even have that much freedom?

274
00:21:48,920 --> 00:21:49,960
I'm just following orders.

275
00:21:50,000 --> 00:21:52,119
Or you could go in and ask him yourself.

276
00:21:58,440 --> 00:21:59,798
I'll hand it over once
we're back in my room.

277
00:21:59,799 --> 00:22:00,799
Is that alright?

278
00:22:01,960 --> 00:22:03,799
Nothing happened just now, right?

279
00:22:06,960 --> 00:22:08,399
What could've happened to me?

280
00:22:08,400 --> 00:22:09,480
What are you talking about?

281
00:22:11,039 --> 00:22:12,039
Good.

282
00:22:12,200 --> 00:22:13,160
Because if something had happened,

283
00:22:13,161 --> 00:22:14,841
you wouldn't need to hand over your phone.

284
00:22:16,000 --> 00:22:16,960
What do you mean?

285
00:22:16,961 --> 00:22:18,761
Because you'd be
allowed to leave right away.

286
00:22:21,640 --> 00:22:24,880
Then... does what just happened count?

287
00:22:41,279 --> 00:22:42,559
"Dear Xiaobei,"

288
00:22:43,079 --> 00:22:44,199
"Mom took"

289
00:22:44,200 --> 00:22:46,160
"a very expensive ring
from my employer's house,"

290
00:22:46,960 --> 00:22:49,279
"so I have to go away for a while."

291
00:22:49,440 --> 00:22:51,200
"Take good care of
your brother and sister."

292
00:22:51,240 --> 00:22:53,440
"If Master P'Eng from the
employer's family finds you,"

293
00:22:53,680 --> 00:22:54,359
"remember:"

294
00:22:54,599 --> 00:22:56,440
"you must stay in his house at all costs."

295
00:22:56,759 --> 00:22:57,759
"No matter what."

296
00:22:58,680 --> 00:23:00,800
Is she offering me as
collateral to pay off her debt?

297
00:23:01,119 --> 00:23:02,720
What kind of mother does that?

298
00:23:06,480 --> 00:23:09,119
Wait, something feels off.

299
00:23:09,720 --> 00:23:11,720
This doesn't sound like
Mom's usual tone at all.

300
00:23:13,119 --> 00:23:14,720
Things are so urgent,

301
00:23:15,200 --> 00:23:17,680
yet she took the time to
use perfect punctuation?

302
00:23:18,000 --> 00:23:19,119
That's really fishy.

303
00:23:19,359 --> 00:23:20,160
Don't worry.

304
00:23:20,161 --> 00:23:21,495
I'm only holding onto it temporarily.

305
00:23:21,519 --> 00:23:22,920
I won't snoop through your phone.

306
00:23:28,160 --> 00:23:30,119
Let me send one last text to A Pong,

307
00:23:30,440 --> 00:23:31,798
telling him not to worry about me

308
00:23:31,799 --> 00:23:33,295
and to look after my brother and sister.

309
00:23:33,319 --> 00:23:34,319
Alright.

310
00:23:34,920 --> 00:23:36,559
Do you need me to make a trip

311
00:23:36,839 --> 00:23:38,400
to grab some daily essentials for you?

312
00:23:39,920 --> 00:23:40,480
Oh, right.

313
00:23:40,481 --> 00:23:41,559
You can contact A Pong.

314
00:23:41,759 --> 00:23:43,000
He knows what I need.

315
00:23:43,680 --> 00:23:45,159
Have him pack things up

316
00:23:45,160 --> 00:23:46,319
and bring them over.

317
00:23:47,960 --> 00:23:48,480
Understood.

318
00:23:48,599 --> 00:23:49,599
I'll arrange it tomorrow.

319
00:23:55,839 --> 00:23:56,839
Mr. Mingkun,

320
00:23:58,720 --> 00:24:00,519
may I ask you something?

321
00:24:00,960 --> 00:24:02,119
Sure, go ahead.

322
00:24:04,319 --> 00:24:06,440
In Master P'Eng's room,

323
00:24:07,559 --> 00:24:09,119
there's an old,

324
00:24:09,400 --> 00:24:11,039
kind of ugly plushie.

325
00:24:11,200 --> 00:24:13,000
Is that thing really important to him?

326
00:24:13,200 --> 00:24:14,280
How do you know about that?

327
00:24:14,759 --> 00:24:16,920
Did the Master show it to you?

328
00:24:18,799 --> 00:24:19,400
No.

329
00:24:19,599 --> 00:24:21,680
I just caught a glimpse of it by accident.

330
00:24:21,720 --> 00:24:24,000
That's very precious to the Young Master.

331
00:24:25,160 --> 00:24:27,359
It was the last gift the
Madame left for him.

332
00:24:29,079 --> 00:24:29,519
By the way,

333
00:24:29,759 --> 00:24:31,319
please be up early tomorrow.

334
00:24:32,440 --> 00:24:33,639
Master P'Eng asked

335
00:24:33,640 --> 00:24:35,759
that you prepare a
Chinese breakfast for two.

336
00:24:42,079 --> 00:24:45,359
So the guy actually saved a portion for me.

337
00:24:45,680 --> 00:24:46,960
How thoughtful.

338
00:24:54,640 --> 00:24:55,960
So, what you're saying is

339
00:24:56,680 --> 00:24:59,118
you want me to let him go home?

340
00:24:59,119 --> 00:24:59,559
Yes.

341
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:01,440
Exactly as Boss P'Eng understood.

342
00:25:04,000 --> 00:25:05,000
You see,

343
00:25:05,759 --> 00:25:07,720
these two kids are his younger siblings.

344
00:25:08,039 --> 00:25:09,318
They're still so young.

345
00:25:09,319 --> 00:25:12,142
Their parents are both gone, leaving
them all alone. It's heartbreaking.

346
00:25:13,519 --> 00:25:14,799
Alright, I got it.

347
00:25:16,400 --> 00:25:17,400
Let's talk about you.

348
00:25:18,559 --> 00:25:19,559
Oh.

349
00:25:23,480 --> 00:25:24,240
Boss P'Eng,

350
00:25:24,359 --> 00:25:26,359
do you usually eat this for breakfast?

351
00:25:33,559 --> 00:25:35,880
So that's what he meant
by 'breakfast for two.'

352
00:25:38,400 --> 00:25:39,400
No.

353
00:25:39,720 --> 00:25:40,920
It was made specially for you.

354
00:25:43,599 --> 00:25:46,599
Pao Bei got up at four in the
morning to prepare all this.

355
00:25:47,920 --> 00:25:49,440
Thank you for your hard work, Pao Bei.

356
00:25:51,119 --> 00:25:52,960
I'm in for a treat today.

357
00:25:53,400 --> 00:25:55,320
Thank you for your warm
hospitality, Boss P'Eng.

358
00:25:55,359 --> 00:25:57,559
It makes this foreign
visitor feel right at home.

359
00:25:58,079 --> 00:25:59,480
A true celebrity.

360
00:25:59,920 --> 00:26:02,079
I could never match that
eloquence and charm.

361
00:26:03,480 --> 00:26:04,480
Try some.

362
00:26:06,200 --> 00:26:07,599
This steamed bun looks great.

363
00:26:14,960 --> 00:26:15,960
What's the filling?

364
00:26:16,519 --> 00:26:18,839
It feels familiar yet new.

365
00:26:19,680 --> 00:26:20,680
The texture is wonderful.

366
00:26:21,960 --> 00:26:23,599
It's stuffed with cauliflower and tofu.

367
00:26:25,200 --> 00:26:26,439
It's my first time trying this.

368
00:26:26,440 --> 00:26:27,440
It's delicious.

369
00:26:30,680 --> 00:26:31,680
Boss P'Eng,

370
00:26:31,920 --> 00:26:33,680
why not let Pao Bei sit down and join us?

371
00:26:33,920 --> 00:26:34,920
He worked hard on this.

372
00:26:34,960 --> 00:26:35,960
No need.

373
00:26:36,559 --> 00:26:37,999
We have our own business to discuss.

374
00:26:39,920 --> 00:26:40,920
Dismiss everyone.

375
00:26:41,119 --> 00:26:42,119
Yes, sir.

376
00:26:45,279 --> 00:26:46,279
Hey, you.

377
00:26:46,720 --> 00:26:47,720
Wait.

378
00:26:52,640 --> 00:26:53,640
Give him his phone.

379
00:26:53,759 --> 00:26:54,759
Let him go home.

380
00:26:57,599 --> 00:27:00,200
"If Master P'Eng from the
employer's family finds you,"

381
00:27:00,559 --> 00:27:01,240
"remember:"

382
00:27:01,241 --> 00:27:03,079
"you must stay in his house at all costs."

383
00:27:03,240 --> 00:27:04,240
"No matter what."

384
00:27:06,119 --> 00:27:07,119
I'm not leaving.

385
00:27:10,960 --> 00:27:11,960
Suit yourself.

386
00:27:16,920 --> 00:27:18,440
Where were we?

387
00:27:35,759 --> 00:27:37,200
Are you really letting him leave?

388
00:27:42,279 --> 00:27:43,519
He won't leave.

389
00:27:53,599 --> 00:27:54,599
"Give him his phone."

390
00:27:54,640 --> 00:27:55,640
"Let him go home."

391
00:27:57,119 --> 00:27:58,119
"I'm not leaving."

392
00:28:02,079 --> 00:28:03,079
"Suit yourself."

393
00:28:03,599 --> 00:28:05,640
What the hell does he mean by that?

394
00:28:06,000 --> 00:28:07,280
Just casting me aside like this?

395
00:28:07,400 --> 00:28:08,400
What do you take me for?

396
00:28:08,480 --> 00:28:09,480
Some kind of gigolo?

397
00:28:11,559 --> 00:28:12,799
Screw this, I'm done!

398
00:28:14,200 --> 00:28:15,520
Let someone else put up with him!

399
00:28:18,319 --> 00:28:20,159
Look at you, full of fire
on an empty stomach.

400
00:28:23,079 --> 00:28:24,735
Your steamed buns are genuinely delicious.

401
00:28:24,759 --> 00:28:25,640
You've been busy all morning.

402
00:28:25,680 --> 00:28:26,680
Come have some too.

403
00:28:27,480 --> 00:28:28,480
I'm fine, not hungry.

404
00:28:34,480 --> 00:28:35,839
Full from anger, are we?

405
00:28:36,279 --> 00:28:37,640
What do you think he's playing at?

406
00:28:37,880 --> 00:28:39,039
What does he take me for?

407
00:28:39,279 --> 00:28:41,118
Who does he think he
is, dismissing me like that?

408
00:28:41,119 --> 00:28:41,960
It was just a few kisses!

409
00:28:41,960 --> 00:28:42,960
What's the big deal?

410
00:28:50,519 --> 00:28:51,598
Wait, that's...

411
00:28:51,599 --> 00:28:52,959
Forget it, drop it.

412
00:28:52,960 --> 00:28:53,960
I get your point.

413
00:28:54,599 --> 00:28:57,119
So you're really not leaving?

414
00:28:58,440 --> 00:28:59,440
Hell no, I'm not leaving!

415
00:28:59,960 --> 00:29:01,200
I need an explanation from him!

416
00:29:01,839 --> 00:29:02,839
Mm.

417
00:29:02,920 --> 00:29:05,200
Though you might
have to wait until tonight.

418
00:29:05,440 --> 00:29:07,079
You still have a day's work to do here.

419
00:29:07,400 --> 00:29:08,160
Huh?

420
00:29:08,160 --> 00:29:09,160
Is he going out?

421
00:29:09,319 --> 00:29:09,880
Yes.

422
00:29:10,240 --> 00:29:11,240
He's taking Milan out.

423
00:29:25,079 --> 00:29:26,278
What is his deal anyway?

424
00:29:26,279 --> 00:29:27,279
A grown man,

425
00:29:27,440 --> 00:29:29,360
does he always need
someone keeping him company?

426
00:29:29,559 --> 00:29:31,440
One person yesterday, another today.

427
00:29:31,680 --> 00:29:32,960
Can't he just be alone for once?

428
00:30:32,079 --> 00:30:33,079
Young Master.

429
00:30:33,559 --> 00:30:34,039
Young Master.

430
00:30:34,040 --> 00:30:35,200
I'll take you to get changed.

431
00:30:36,039 --> 00:30:37,039
Young M...

432
00:30:38,920 --> 00:30:39,920
Don't walk away!

433
00:30:40,440 --> 00:30:41,640
You wait right here!

434
00:30:42,559 --> 00:30:44,400
Fine, Master P'Eng.

435
00:31:06,920 --> 00:31:07,920
Come in.

436
00:31:09,640 --> 00:31:10,359
Pao Bei,

437
00:31:10,519 --> 00:31:12,480
there are a few things
I need to brief you on.

438
00:31:14,240 --> 00:31:15,039
Go ahead.

439
00:31:15,040 --> 00:31:17,200
You said you wanted to take on more work,

440
00:31:17,440 --> 00:31:18,758
but this place is huge.

441
00:31:18,759 --> 00:31:20,000
You can't handle it all alone.

442
00:31:20,599 --> 00:31:21,720
The Master instructed

443
00:31:21,880 --> 00:31:22,919
that you only need to clean

444
00:31:22,920 --> 00:31:24,640
the areas where he spends most of his time.

445
00:31:26,400 --> 00:31:27,519
What does that mean?

446
00:31:27,880 --> 00:31:30,440
He specifically ordered me to
clean the places he frequents?

447
00:31:32,119 --> 00:31:32,480
Yes.

448
00:31:32,559 --> 00:31:34,880
He made a point to say
that right before heading out.

449
00:31:37,880 --> 00:31:39,160
Didn't he just tell me to scram?

450
00:31:39,599 --> 00:31:40,719
Now he's pulling this stunt.

451
00:31:42,079 --> 00:31:43,279
I really can't figure him out.

452
00:31:44,400 --> 00:31:45,400
Neither can I.

453
00:31:50,559 --> 00:31:51,758
Mr. Mingkun,

454
00:31:51,759 --> 00:31:53,200
I really admire you.

455
00:31:54,839 --> 00:31:55,839
Admire me for what?

456
00:31:57,799 --> 00:31:59,399
Working for that monster...

457
00:31:59,400 --> 00:32:00,680
how long have you been with him?

458
00:32:02,119 --> 00:32:03,558
We grew up together,

459
00:32:03,559 --> 00:32:04,559
right up to now.

460
00:32:06,039 --> 00:32:07,799
Then honestly, I admire you even more.

461
00:32:08,319 --> 00:32:10,400
Haven't you ever thought about leaving

462
00:32:10,480 --> 00:32:11,919
to do what you actually want to do?

463
00:32:11,920 --> 00:32:14,078
Why don't we partner up on something?

464
00:32:14,079 --> 00:32:15,799
Let's not stay here and let him torture us!

465
00:32:17,799 --> 00:32:20,680
My parents and I have
dedicated our lives to this family.

466
00:32:20,920 --> 00:32:22,359
I have no intention of leaving.

467
00:32:24,599 --> 00:32:25,879
That's such a shame.

468
00:32:25,880 --> 00:32:27,358
With your patience and resilience,

469
00:32:27,359 --> 00:32:29,399
you could succeed at
anything you set your mind to.

470
00:32:30,680 --> 00:32:32,000
You're quite impressive yourself.

471
00:32:32,680 --> 00:32:34,598
You should know, those
permitted by the Master

472
00:32:34,599 --> 00:32:36,359
to enter his room and clean

473
00:32:36,920 --> 00:32:37,920
are few and far between.

474
00:32:40,079 --> 00:32:43,319
Then who cleaned it before I got here?

475
00:32:48,279 --> 00:32:49,160
It was me.

476
00:32:49,160 --> 00:32:50,160
Right.

477
00:32:51,440 --> 00:32:53,239
So I should be thanking you

478
00:32:53,240 --> 00:32:54,720
for taking so much work off my hands.

479
00:32:56,160 --> 00:32:57,160
Keep it up.

480
00:32:57,359 --> 00:32:58,679
I have other things to attend to.

481
00:33:01,440 --> 00:33:02,039
Alright.

482
00:33:02,240 --> 00:33:03,279
Leave it to me!

483
00:33:06,000 --> 00:33:07,400
I need to learn from Mingkun,

484
00:33:07,559 --> 00:33:09,119
learn to adapt and endure.

485
00:33:09,720 --> 00:33:10,720
I definitely can't leave.

486
00:33:11,440 --> 00:33:12,960
I can't let him get his way so easily.

487
00:33:13,920 --> 00:33:16,160
Besides, didn't Mom tell me
to stay here no matter what?

488
00:33:16,720 --> 00:33:19,039
She must have had a reason.

489
00:33:19,960 --> 00:33:22,599
Could it be related to that secret room?

490
00:33:23,400 --> 00:33:25,840
Given the chance, I'm definitely
sneaking in to check it out.

491
00:33:25,960 --> 00:33:27,359
If I find dirt on that monster,

492
00:33:28,079 --> 00:33:29,880
he won't dare bully me ever again.

493
00:33:48,680 --> 00:33:49,680
What's this?

494
00:34:05,119 --> 00:34:08,159
Technology really does
make life easier, huh?

495
00:34:08,679 --> 00:34:10,000
This thing is so convenient!

496
00:34:34,639 --> 00:34:35,639
Ow, that hurts!

497
00:34:36,920 --> 00:34:38,280
What did I do to deserve this?

498
00:34:39,320 --> 00:34:40,760
This room is definitely cursed.

499
00:34:41,519 --> 00:34:43,639
I'm getting out of here as
soon as I finish sweeping.

500
00:34:50,079 --> 00:34:51,079
It broke!

501
00:35:04,000 --> 00:35:05,079
Don't panic.

502
00:35:08,159 --> 00:35:09,159
Glue.

503
00:35:09,519 --> 00:35:10,519
Find some glue.

504
00:35:30,960 --> 00:35:32,279
"That's something"

505
00:35:32,280 --> 00:35:33,720
"very precious to the Young Master."

506
00:35:34,400 --> 00:35:36,480
"It was the last gift the
Madame left for him."

507
00:35:50,320 --> 00:35:51,320
Listen carefully:

508
00:35:51,679 --> 00:35:53,639
Only the Young Master
is allowed in this room.

509
00:35:54,199 --> 00:35:56,320
Anyone else who enters without permission

510
00:35:56,599 --> 00:35:58,320
will face severe consequences.

511
00:35:59,440 --> 00:36:02,799
The key to that secret
room must be in here.

512
00:36:02,800 --> 00:36:04,079
Just you wait.

513
00:36:04,159 --> 00:36:05,719
One day, I'll uncover all your secrets.

514
00:36:08,360 --> 00:36:10,199
Glue...

515
00:36:10,400 --> 00:36:11,400
There's no time.

516
00:36:11,480 --> 00:36:12,520
I have to find glue first.

517
00:36:49,079 --> 00:36:51,199
Why did the two of them come back together?

518
00:36:51,519 --> 00:36:52,519
Don't tell me they...

519
00:36:52,960 --> 00:36:53,960
they...

520
00:36:54,360 --> 00:36:55,639
What a shameless playboy!

521
00:37:04,559 --> 00:37:05,639
Pao Bei.

522
00:37:05,960 --> 00:37:06,960
Pao Bei!

523
00:37:09,000 --> 00:37:09,800
Pao Bei!

524
00:37:09,920 --> 00:37:12,639
The Master wants you to go to his room.

525
00:37:13,039 --> 00:37:14,119
What does he want now?

526
00:37:14,599 --> 00:37:16,760
Didn't he bring someone home already?

527
00:37:17,599 --> 00:37:18,639
Looking for trouble again.

528
00:37:21,599 --> 00:37:22,639
Just my luck.

529
00:37:38,679 --> 00:37:39,760
What do you want?

530
00:37:41,320 --> 00:37:42,519
Did he find out?

531
00:37:42,920 --> 00:37:44,119
Probably not.

532
00:37:44,400 --> 00:37:45,558
I glued it back so securely.

533
00:37:45,559 --> 00:37:46,999
I tugged on it over and
over, and it didn't budge.

534
00:37:47,000 --> 00:37:48,119
There's no way he noticed.

535
00:37:48,960 --> 00:37:50,079
Right, impossible.

536
00:37:50,400 --> 00:37:51,800
I shouldn't psych myself out.

537
00:37:52,119 --> 00:37:53,239
You call me over

538
00:37:53,320 --> 00:37:54,615
and don't say a word. What's the deal?

539
00:37:54,639 --> 00:37:56,079
Who gave you permission to touch it?

540
00:37:59,760 --> 00:38:00,760
Touch what?

541
00:38:02,159 --> 00:38:03,480
Did you touch this?

542
00:38:07,119 --> 00:38:08,119
Yeah, I did.

543
00:38:15,719 --> 00:38:17,239
Get your revenge if you must.

544
00:38:17,440 --> 00:38:18,960
First you spilled water,

545
00:38:19,559 --> 00:38:20,800
and now you broke my stuff?

546
00:38:21,880 --> 00:38:22,800
Broke it? I—.

547
00:38:22,801 --> 00:38:24,000
Still denying it?

548
00:38:26,880 --> 00:38:27,880
Do you take me for an idiot?

549
00:38:27,881 --> 00:38:30,041
You think I can't tell right-side
up from upside down?

550
00:38:34,840 --> 00:38:36,600
How was I supposed to
know which way was up?

551
00:38:40,960 --> 00:38:41,800
The spilled water,

552
00:38:41,960 --> 00:38:43,000
I let that slide.

553
00:38:43,519 --> 00:38:45,079
And now you break my belongings?

554
00:38:46,280 --> 00:38:47,360
I didn't do it on purpose!

555
00:38:47,880 --> 00:38:49,439
I just wanted to glue it back together!

556
00:38:49,440 --> 00:38:50,760
Can't tell which way is up, huh?

557
00:38:52,159 --> 00:38:53,159
Fine.

558
00:38:54,079 --> 00:38:55,079
Let me teach you.

559
00:38:56,719 --> 00:38:57,719
What are you doing?

560
00:38:58,199 --> 00:38:58,920
Let go of me!

561
00:38:58,960 --> 00:38:59,599
What do you want?

562
00:38:59,599 --> 00:39:00,599
Let go of me!

563
00:39:00,679 --> 00:39:01,679
Put me down!

564
00:39:01,960 --> 00:39:02,960
Mingkun, help me!

565
00:39:03,039 --> 00:39:04,400
Your master has gone crazy again!

566
00:39:04,519 --> 00:39:05,280
Mingkun, save me!

567
00:39:05,440 --> 00:39:06,800
Mingkun, help me!

568
00:39:07,760 --> 00:39:08,760
Mingkun!

569
00:39:11,079 --> 00:39:12,119
Let go of me!

570
00:39:18,480 --> 00:39:19,480
What is your problem?

571
00:39:23,360 --> 00:39:24,039
If you want to play around,

572
00:39:24,040 --> 00:39:25,360
couldn't you be a little gentler?

573
00:39:44,079 --> 00:39:45,079
Scared now?

574
00:39:45,920 --> 00:39:47,000
Dare to mess with me again?

575
00:39:47,199 --> 00:39:48,320
I'm not scared of you!

576
00:39:48,519 --> 00:39:49,760
I'm not afraid of you at all!

577
00:39:54,199 --> 00:39:55,238
Call me daddy.

578
00:39:55,239 --> 00:39:56,639
Call me daddy and I'll forgive you.

579
00:40:00,719 --> 00:40:01,719
What are you laughing at?

580
00:40:04,639 --> 00:40:07,320
I'm laughing at how childish you are.

581
00:40:08,719 --> 00:40:09,800
What did you say?

582
00:40:11,920 --> 00:40:15,320
Only a little kid would ask
someone to call him daddy.

583
00:40:25,840 --> 00:40:26,840
Keep going!

584
00:40:26,960 --> 00:40:28,000
Why did you stop?

585
00:40:28,559 --> 00:40:29,679
Is that all you've got?
